# https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#MechanicalPerformanceParameter> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Aggregated observed mechanical performance parameter describing the strength of a fabric, potentially covering tensile strength, tear strength or bursting strength depending on the test context."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fabric strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#evidenceStatus> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#explicitEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "Fabric strength contributes to the interpretation of intrinsic durability as an aggregated mechanical performance parameter."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "Fabric strength is modelled as reducing the likelihood of tear or rip under comparable conditions, rather than as negatively affecting tear or rip."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricStrength> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Annex 13.10.1, printed page 468, lines 11065-11071; Annex 13.4, Table 124, printed pages 362-367 where applicable."@en .
