# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#SurfaceDegradationPhenomenon> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Observed surface degradation phenomenon involving fuzzing or matting of the fabric surface. The term follows the JRC and ISO wording 'fuzzing or matting', not 'melting'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fuzzing or matting"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Fabric fuzzing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Fabric matting"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#evidenceStatus> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#explicitEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "FuzzingOrMatting is not made a subclass of FailureMode because it is modelled following the existing pilling pattern as an observed degradation phenomenon used in performance inspection."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "The research gap used the wording 'fuzzing/melting', but the JRC and referenced ISO standards use fuzzing/matting. This ontology therefore introduces FuzzingOrMatting and avoids the unsupported term melting."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "CIRPASS Textile Ontology modelling specification, version 1.1.0."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingAbstraction> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FuzzingOrMatting> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#typicalProgressionTo> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#FabricBreakdown> .
